<article class="env-lemma" id="098D">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/098D">Lemma <span data-tag="098D">61.12.5</span>.</a> Let $T$ be an affine scheme. Let $\{ T_ i \to T\} _{i \in I}$ be a pro-étale covering of $T$. Then there exists a pro-étale covering $\{ U_ j \to T\} _{j = 1, \ldots , n}$ which is a refinement of $\{ T_ i \to T\} _{i \in I}$ such that each $U_ j$ is an affine scheme. Moreover, we may choose each $U_ j$ to be open affine in one of the $T_ i$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      This follows directly from the definition. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>